    "body": "## Motivation\n\n- **Crash:** `copy_mla_rows_into_pack` launches its gather kernel with\n  `grid=(num_layers, cdiv(n*max_item_len, 1024))`, putting the n-dependent\n  dimension on `grid.y` (hardware cap 65,535). Any pack above **58,253\n  rows** (at 1152 B/row) fails launch with\n  `RuntimeError: Triton Error [CUDA]: invalid argument`, killing the\n  mooncake transfer worker thread silently and stalling cross-node KV\n  transfer with zero error logs. This makes chunked-prefill-size 65536\n  unusable while 16384 works, for reasons unrelated to model or memory.\n- **Throughput:** the upstream kernel moves **one byte per lane**; measured\n  ~510-550 GB/s on B300 — far from memory-bound, so the pack step\n  needlessly inflates PD transfer latency for large windows.\n\n## Modifications\n\n- **Swap grid dims:** blocks on `grid.x` (limit 2^31-1), layers on\n  `grid.y` (a few dozen at most). Kernel logic unchanged; no div/mod.\n- **Vectorize to 8-byte lanes:** when every `item_len` and\n  `src_item_len` is 8-aligned (MLA item lengths are 1152 B — the common\n  case), gather through an int64 view of the pack buffer. Non-8-aligned\n  item lengths fall back to the (dim-swapped) byte path, preserving\n  original behavior.\n- **Opt-in int64 addressing:** enabled only when the launch size actually\n  approaches 2^31, avoiding int64's cost in the common case.\n- Merged with the upstream `src_row_stride` / `src_token_item_lens`\n  parameters (strided source rows are honored by both paths).\n\n## Accuracy Tests\n\n- `test/registered/kernels/test_pd_dcp_gather.py` (CUDA, registered\n  `base-b-kernel-unit` / `1-gpu-large`): byte-exact pack vs a reference\n  gather at n = 1,000 / 58,253 / 100,000 / 300,000 rows (2 layers x\n  1152 B); strided-source case (`src_item_len=1536`); byte-path case with\n  `item_len=1001` (non-8-aligned); a direct-launch case compiling and\n  running the `USE_INT64=True` branch. All 7 cases pass. The upstream\n  kernel crashes at n=100,000 with the exact production signature,\n  validating the test.\n- Production validation: full-model (93-layer Kimi-K3) PD+DCP rounds at\n  chunk 65536 (2x 30-min, c32, 2,436 requests, 0 errors, 0 transfer\n  failures) with this kernel in the transfer path, plus a 12-question\n  gsm8k probe afterwards (acc=1.000, invalid=0.000).\n\n## Speed Tests and Profiling\n\n**Setup.** B300 GPU, 2 layers x 1152 B/row (production MLA shape),\nCUDA-event `do_bench`, min over 50 reps, idle GPU, 5 repeated rounds per\npoint.\n\n| rows | original (upstream) | this MR (vec8) | vs original |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| 16,384 | ~509 GB/s | 1,872-1,887 | **+268%** |\n| 32,768 | ~538 | 2,262-2,311 | **+327%** |\n| 58,253 | ~549 | 2,577-2,591 | **+372%** |\n| 100,000 | **CRASH** (grid.y=112,500) | 2,786-2,792 | — |\n| 300,000 | **CRASH** (grid.y=337,500) | 3,004-3,005 | — |\n\nBlock-size sweep for the vec8 path: 512 elements/block wins (2,369 /\n**3,005** / 2,336 GB/s at 300K rows for 256/512/2048). Grid-swap-only\n(V2) lands at ~488-528 GB/s, i.e. correctness without the throughput\ngain; 1D-flatten variants measured -12~-14% vs original in earlier\nrounds.\n\n## Checklist\n\n- [x] Format your code according to the Format code with pre-commit guide\n      (pre-commit passes on all touched files).\n- [x] Add unit tests according to the Run and add unit tests guide\n      (CUDA, registered; see above).\n- [x] Update documentation according to the Write documentations guide\n      (no user-facing config change; N/A).\n- [x] Provide accuracy and speed benchmark results (see sections above).\n- [x] Follow the SGLang code style guidance.\n\n<!-- pr-states:start -->\n---\n### CI States\n\nLatest PR Test (Base): <!-- slot:pr-test:start -->:x: [Run #38213764653](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/actions/runs/38213764653)<!-- slot:pr-test:end -->\nLatest PR Test (Extra): <!-- slot:pr-test-extra:start -->:x: [Run #38213764110](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/actions/runs/38213764110)<!-- slot:pr-test-extra:end -->\nLatest PR Test (AMD ROCm 10): <!-- slot:pr-test-amd:start -->:x: [Run #38213764269](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/actions/runs/38213764269)<!-- slot:pr-test-amd:end -->\n<!-- pr-states:end -->",
